Source: @FIPSPKG@
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: OpenSSL Packages <openssl-packages@openssl.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 12~), perl
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://openssl-library.org

Package: @FIPSPKG@
Architecture: any
XB-Packaging-Commit: @PACKAGING_COMMIT@
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenSSL FIPS provider for the @MODDIR@ stream (upstream build, not validated)
 The OpenSSL FIPS provider module (fips.so) built from the same source
 release as the openssl@MODDIR@-upstream packages, with `enable-fips` and
 nothing else, installed at /opt/openssl/fips/@MODDIR@/fips.so. It upgrades
 in step with the @MODDIR@ stream, so it always matches the stream's
 current source.
 .
 This module is NOT NIST-validated. It enforces approved-only algorithms —
 useful for developing and testing FIPS-mode behaviour — but it does not
 make an installation FIPS 140-3 compliant. For compliance, install a
 validated openssl-fips<version>-upstream package instead.
 .
 Activate it for a stream on the deployment machine, e.g.:
   /opt/openssl/@MODDIR@/bin/openssl-fips-enable @MODDIR@
 On upgrade the module is re-activated automatically for any stream that
 has it enabled, so its integrity checksum keeps matching the new bytes.
